{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"5181fd300c667dcb63172792ef99f705d84835d18799498dd6a03e82f0307cf9","digest":{"component_or_area":"op-cert attestation signing and verification","key_entities":["plan-review","completion-verifier","src/rebar/attest/hmac_legacy.py","attest/registry.py","signing.sign_manifest","signing.compute_signature","verify_signature","sign_result.schema.json","docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md","rebar.authorship.v1"],"problem_keywords":["hmac removal","op-cert migration","legacy scheme deprecation","asymmetric signing","contract phase"],"propositions":["Remove HMAC-SHA256 scheme registration for plan-review and completion-verifier kinds from attest/registry.py POLICY so they no longer resolve to the HMAC signing method.","Delete the HMAC branch in signing.sign_manifest for op-cert kinds, leaving only the asymmetric envelope path; signing.compute_signature and .signing-key remain untouched for non-op-cert consumers.","Pre-existing HMAC attestations for op-cert kinds must read as not-certified post-contract while remaining preserved in the event log; re-running the gate re-issues valid Ed25519 op-certs without rewriting history.","Create docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md with Expand and Contract sections, including cutover procedure (reconcile hosts first) and re-issue procedure for stale HMAC attestations.","Verify the asymmetric producer path (expand phase) is present before removal via import check and end-to-end op-cert sign/verify smoke test.","Authorship kind and non-op-cert HMAC consumers must remain untouched and continue to verify correctly post-removal."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785821809332119230,"uuid":"14801af2-592a-42de-a436-c807503504fc"}